	<description>The comical, fantastical, romantical, (not) entirely true story of Lady Jane Grey. In &lt;i&gt;My Lady Jane&lt;/i&gt;, coauthors Cynthia Hand, Brodi Ashton, and Jodi Meadows have created a one-of-a-kind fantasy in the tradition of &lt;i&gt;The Princess Bride&lt;/i&gt;, featuring a reluctant king, an even more reluctant queen, a noble steed, and only a passing resemblance to actual history—because sometimes history needs a little help.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;At sixteen, Lady Jane Grey is about to be married off to a stranger and caught up in a conspiracy to rob her cousin, King Edward, of his throne. But those trifling problems aren’t for Jane to worry about. Jane is about to become the Queen of England.</description>
